<title>USA: Dow gains more than 100 points.</title>
<headline>Dow gains more than 100 points.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dow Jones industrial average gained more than 100 points in late afternoon trading Tuesday as the market extended its recovery from Monday's 192-point plunge on comments by Japan's prime minister about a possible sale of U.S. Treasuries.</p>
<p>Shortly after 2:45 p.m. EDT, the index of 30 blue-chip issues was up 114.90 points at 7,719.16.</p>
